Intended to be an "implementation detail" for SDL3 that implements various *NIX functionalities without inflating the main SDL3 library.
Its primarily designed to avoid GLib/GObject solely due to state corruption and symbol conflict issues.
MIT licensed but dynamically links to libraries with other FOSS licenses like ding-libs (ini_config), NSPR4 and Pixman.

Implements:
-Pixman XPM1/XPM2/XPM2 loader
-Pixman SVG loader (PlutoSVG wrapper)
-Pixman PNG codec (spng wrapper)
-XDG Base Directory API
-XDG Icon Theme API (icon filename lookup, loading icons as Pixman images, theme enumeration, fallback icon generation)
-Desktop Settings API (supports both XDG Portals and XSettings)
-Fallback "Unicode" text renderer (uses built in bitmap font)

Planned:
-Maybe allow disabling features or letting inih be used instead of ding-libs
-Documentation
-GIO style "get icon representation of a file system object" API
-Unicode text renderer (wrapper around FreeType2 +FontConfig + HarfBuzz ala libfcft)
-Move the fallback toolkit (SDL3 PR #15375, rewrite of X11TK) into here
-Toolkit wrapper around the fallback one, sandboxed (fork() + dynamic loading + IPC SHM, for avoiding GLib/GObject issues) GTK2/3/4  
 and sandboxed Qt (seperate library that will provide basic C API for Qt5/Qt6/TQt functions)
-Minimal embedded Wayland compositor for embedding GTK/Qt menubars into SDL safely
